{"kind":"finding","id":"F-io-serialization-001-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/GuiTreeAssemblerTests.cs","line":791,"method":"TheRectSlackIsAnUpperBoundNotJustALowerOne","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GuiTreeModel.cs:219 LayoutGroupContainmentSlackPx 4f->40f; this cell stays GREEN while MissingEndVerticalIsRecoveredFromRectContainment (line 293) goes red","what_it_asserts":"A child rect offset by slack-1 px keeps a LayoutGroup open and one offset by slack+1 px closes it, with both offsets computed from GuiTreeAssembler.LayoutGroupContainmentSlackPx.","why_weak":"The comment at lines 793-797 claims an accidental slack change reds here. Because both sides are derived from the constant, any slack value satisfies both assertions; the cell pins the relational contract, not the value.","proposed_action":"Either add one absolute-value assertion (Assert.Equal(4f, GuiTreeAssembler.LayoutGroupContainmentSlackPx)) or reword the comment to say the value itself is pinned by MissingEndVerticalIsRecoveredFromRectContainment.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
